🔹 1. Initialization
Step 1: Set front = -1 and rear = -1


🔹 2. Enqueue Operation (Insertion)
Step 1: Check if queue is full
        IF ( (rear + 1) % n == front )
            PRINT "Overflow" and EXIT

Step 2: IF (front == -1 AND rear == -1)
            front = 0
            rear = 0
        ELSE
            rear = (rear + 1) % n

Step 3: queue[rear] = value
Step 4: PRINT value inserted



🔹 3. Dequeue Operation (Deletion)
Step 1: Check if queue is empty
        IF (front == -1)
            PRINT "Underflow" and EXIT

Step 2: STORE queue[front] in temp

Step 3: IF (front == rear)
            front = -1
            rear = -1
        ELSE
            front = (front + 1) % n

Step 4: PRINT temp deleted


🔹 4. Display Queue
Step 1: IF (front == -1)
            PRINT "Queue is Empty" and EXIT

Step 2: SET i = front

Step 3: WHILE (i != rear)
            PRINT queue[i]
            i = (i + 1) % n

Step 4: PRINT queue[rear]
